tus code (404 GET https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/blob/main/docs/custom-provider.md)"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "tool_b49PmA5u498GIP09OxjB7VnU", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "bash", "arguments": "{\"command\":\"find ~/.config/opencode -name \\\"*.md\\\" -o -name \\\"*.txt\\\" 2>/dev/null | head -20\",\"description\":\"Find docs in opencode config\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "tool_b49PmA5u498GIP09OxjB7VnU", "content": "[Old tool result content cleared]"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "tool_yvoyIOlwHuw4vdlZgU8PSuWV", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "bash", "arguments": "{\"command\":\"cat ~/.config/opencode/agents/swen3.md\",\"description\":\"Check swen3 agent config\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "tool_yvoyIOlwHuw4vdlZgU8PSuWV", "content": "[Old tool result content cleared]"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I see the current setup uses the agent + tool approach, but the goal is to make opencode use SWEN v3 as the primary LLM provider. Let me check if opencode supports setting a default model in the config.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "tool_Yo1yfBERw6cHxbF1i3j0tHvo", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "bash", "arguments": "{\"command\":\"cat ~/.config/opencode/opencode.json | grep -A5 -B5 \\\"model\\\" || echo \\\"No model field found\\\"\",\"description\":\"Check for model config\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "tool_Yo1yfBERw6cHxbF1i3j0tHvo", "content": "[Old tool result content cleared]"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I need to understand how opencode selects the default model. Let me check the opencode source or docs for the `model` config field.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "tool_qTC7xtXs7KswCln25yGDW5zq", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "webfetch", "arguments": "{\"url\":\"https://opencode.ai/docs/config.json\",\"format\":\"text\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "tool_qTC7xtXs7KswCln25yGDW5zq", "content": "StatusCod