runs locally in Python — no hardware needed.</description>\n    <location>file:///Users/alex/.config/opencode/skills/drone-world-sim/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>git-workflow</name>\n    <description>Помощь в работе с Git — коммиты, ветки, PR, синхронизация с remote</description>\n    <location>file:///Users/alex/.config/opencode/skills/git-workflow/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>github-credentials</name>\n    <description>GitHub authentication credentials for the kis22aem account. Use this skill whenever you need to authenticate with GitHub, push code, create PRs, clone private repos, or perform any Git/GitHub operations that require authentication.</description>\n    <location>file:///Users/alex/.config/opencode/skills/github-credentials/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>github-gem-seeker</name>\n    <description>Search GitHub for battle-tested solutions instead of reinventing the wheel. Use when the user's problem is universal enough that open source developers have probably solved it already—especially for: format conversion (video/audio/image/document), media downloading, file manipulation, web scraping/archiving, automation scripts, and CLI tools. Prefer this skill over writing custom code for well-trodden problems.\n</description>\n    <location>file:///Users/alex/.config/opencode/skills/github-gem-seeker/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>gws-best-practices</name>\n    <description>Best practices for using the gws CLI with supported Google Workspace services (Drive, Docs, Sheets, Slides). Use when performing any operation with the gws CLI.</description>\n    <location>file:///Users/alex/.config/opencode/skills/gws-best-practices/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>igo-ssh-tunnel</name>\n    <description>Instructions and credentials for connecting to the igo-jetson device via the permanent Cloudflare SSH tunnel. Use this skill whenever you need to access t