l result content cleared]"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I see - the provider needs to implement the `LanguageModelV1` interface. However, looking at the opencode docs, it seems like opencode expects providers to export a function that returns a model. Let me check how opencode loads custom providers.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "tool_6534AmKEOSSZANMhzBnnn5TQ", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "bash", "arguments": "{\"command\":\"cat ~/.config/opencode/opencode.json | grep -A 20 '\\\"swen3\\\"'\",\"description\":\"Check swen3 provider config\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "tool_6534AmKEOSSZANMhzBnnn5TQ", "content": "[Old tool result content cleared]"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I see the issue - opencode expects the provider to be an AI SDK compatible package. The `@ai-sdk/openai-compatible` package exports a `createOpenAICompatible` function that returns a provider. I need to make our provider export a similar function.\n\nLet me update the provider to export a function that creates an AI SDK compatible provider.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "tool_C9k1ExbDAcEKENTLH0o2ihAB", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "write", "arguments": "{\"content\":\"import { spawn } from \\\"child_process\\\";\\nimport { ReadableStream } from \\\"stream/web\\\";\\n\\nexport interface Swen3ProviderOptions {\\n  zenohConnect?: string[];\\n  workers?: string[];\\n  timeout?: number;\\n}\\n\\n// System prompt для роя\\nconst SWARM_SYSTEM_PROMPT = `Ты — распределённый рой ИИ-агентов SWEN v3.\\nТы состоишь из нескольких воркеров, которые работают параллельно:\\n- qwen3_5_4b_opus (Diana): сложные задачи, анализ\\n- glm_flash (Diana): код, технические тексты  \\n- jetson_gemma4b (Jetson): простые задачи, факты\\n\\nВсе воркеры получают один и тот же запрос и отвечают независимо.\\nЗатем выбирается лучший ответ.\\n\\nОтвечай на языке запроса пользователя.`;\\n\\nclass Swen3LanguageModel {\\n  readonly specificationVersion = \\\"v1\\\" as const;\\n  readonly provider = \\\"swen3\\\";\\n  readonly modelId = \\\"swarm\\\";\\n  readonly defaultObjectGenerationMode = undefined;\\n  readonly supportsImageUrls = false;\\n  readonly supportsStructuredOutputs = false;\\n\\n  private options: Swen3ProviderOptions;\\n\\n  constructor(options: Swen3ProviderOptions = {}) {\\n    this.options = {\\n      zenohConnect: [\\\"tcp/10.15.64.226:7447\\\", \\\"tcp/10.15.66.12:7447\\\"],\\n      workers: [\\\"glm_flash\\\", \\\"qwen3_5_4b_opus\\\", \\\"jetson_gemma4b\\\"],\\n      timeout: 120000,\\n      ...options,\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n  async doGenerate(options: any): Promise<any> {\\n    const stream = await this.doStream(options);\\n    const chunks: string[] = [];\\n    \\n    const reader = stream.stream.getReader();\\n    while (true) {\\n      const { done, value } = await reader.read();\\n      if (done) break;\\n      chunks.push(value);\\n    }\\n\\n    const text = chunks.join(\\\"\\\");\\n    \\n    return {\\n      text,\\n      finishReason: \\\"stop\\\" as const,\\n      usage: {\\n        promptTokens: 0,\\n        completionTokens: Math.ceil(text.length / 4),\\n      },\\n      rawCall: {\\n        rawPrompt: options.prompt,\\n        rawSettings: {},\\n      },\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n  async doStream(options: any): Promise<any> {\\n    const messages = options.prompt || [];\\n    const lastMessage = messages.filter((m: any) => m.role === \\\"user\\\").pop();\\n    const question = lastMessage?.content || \\\"\\\";\\n\\n    const stream = new ReadableStream({\\n      start: async (controller) => {\\n        try {\\n          controller.enqueue(`🌐 SWEN v3 Swarm Thinking...\\\\n\\\\n`);\\n\\n          const workerStreams = this.options.workers!.map((worker) =>\\n            this.streamWorker(worker, question, controller)\\n          );\\n\\n          await Promise.all(workerStreams);\\n\\n          controller.enqueue(`\\\\n✅ Swarm complete\\\\n`);\\n          controller.close();\\n        } catch (error) {\\n          controller.error(error);\\n        }\\n      },\\n    });\\n\\n    return {\\n      stream,\\n      rawCall: {\\n        rawPrompt: options.prompt,\\n        rawSettings: {},\\n      },\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n  private async streamWorker(\\n    worker: string,\\n    question: string,\\n    controller: ReadableStreamDefaultController<string>\\n  ): Promise<void> {\\n    return new Promise((resolve) => {\\n      const venv = `${process.env.HOME}/.venvs/swen3`;\\n      const script = `${process.env.HOME}/.local/share/swen3/autonomous_swarm.py`;\\n      const python = `${venv}/bin/python3`;\\n\\n      controller.enqueue(`\\\\n🤖 [${worker}] thinking...\\\\n`);\\n\\n      const proc = spawn(python, [script, question], {\\n        env: {\\n          ...process.env,\\n          VIRTUAL_ENV: venv,\\n          PATH: `${venv}/bin:${process.env.PATH}`,\\n          SWEN_WORKERS: worker,\\n        },\\n      });\\n\\n      proc.stdout.on(\\\"data\\\", (data: Buffer) => {\\n        const text = data.toString();\\n        const lines = text.split(\\\"\\\\n\\\");\\n        for (const line of lines) {\\n          if (line.trim() && !line.startsWith(\\\"[Autonomous Swarm]\\\")) {\\n            controller.enqueue(`  ${line}\\\\n`);\\n          }\\n        }\\n      });\\n\\n      proc.stderr.on(\\\"data\\\", (data: Buffer) => {\\n        const text = data.toString();\\n        if (text.includes(\\\"Error\\\")) {\\n          controller.enqueue(`  ❌ Error: ${text.trim()}\\\\n`);\\n        }\\n      });\\n\\n      proc.on(\\\"close\\\", (code) => {\\n        try {\\n          if (code === 0) {\\n            controller.enqueue(`  ✅ [${worker}] done\\\\n`);\\n          } else {\\n            controller.enqueue(`  ❌ [${worker}] failed (code ${code})\\\\n`);\\n          }\\n        } catch (e) {\\n          // Controller already closed, ignore\\n        }\\n        resolve();\\n      });\\n\\n      proc.on(\\\"error\\\", (err) => {\\n        try {\\n          controller.enqueue(`  ❌ [${worker}] error: ${err.message}\\\\n`);\\n        } catch (e) {\\n          // Controller already closed, ignore\\n        }\\n        resolve();\\n      });\\n\\n      setTimeout(() => {\\n        proc.kill();\\n        try {\\n          controller.enqueue(`  ⏱️ [${worker}] timeout\\\\n`);\\n        } catch (e) {\\n          // Controller already closed, ignore\\n        }\\n        resolve();\\n      }, this.options.timeout);\\n    });\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n// Provider factory\\nexport class Swen3Provider {\\n  private options: Swen3ProviderOptions;\\n\\n  constructor(options: Swen3ProviderOptions = {}) {\\n    this.options = options;\\n  }\\n\\n  languageModel(modelId: string): Swen3LanguageModel {\\n    return new Swen3LanguageModel(this.options);\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n// Factory function for AI SDK compatibility\\nexport function createSwen3Provider(options?: Swen3ProviderOptions): Swen3Provider {\\n  return new Swen3Provider(options);\\n}\\n\\n// Default export\\nexport default createSwen3Provider;\\n\",\"filePath\":\"/Users/alex/.local/share/swen3/provider/src/index.ts\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "tool_C9k1ExbDAcEKENTLH0o2ihAB", "content": "[Old tool result content cleared]"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "tool_Xr4bdawnd1HrbjRXEW9ae14c", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "bash", "arguments": "{\"command\":\"cd ~/.local/share/swen3/provider && npm run build\",\"description\":\"Rebuild provider\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "tool_Xr4bdawnd1HrbjRXEW9ae14c", "content": "[Old tool result content cleared]"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "tool_V3UnX7N2f25YbX3DEK0Fa4c9", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "bash", "arguments": "{\"command\":\"node -e \\\"const p = require('/Users/alex/.config/opencode/node_modules/@swen3/provider'); console.log('Provider loaded:', typeof p); console.log('createSwen3Provider:', typeof p.createSwen3Provider); const provider = p.createSwen3Provider(); console.log('languageModel:', typeof provider.languageModel); const model = provider.languageModel('swarm'); console.log('model.specificationVersion:', model.specificationVersion); console.log('model.doGenerate:', typeof model.doGenerate); console.log('model.doStream:', typeof model.doStream);\\\"\",\"description\":\"Test provider interface\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "tool_V3UnX7N2f25YbX3DEK0Fa4c9", "content": "[Old tool result content cleared]"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "The provider now implements the correct interface. However, I realize there might be an issue with how opencode handles the stream. The AI SDK expects the stream to return specific chunks, not just strings. Let me check what format opencode expects for streaming.\n\nActually, looking at the code again, I think the issue might be that opencode expects the provider to work differently. Let me check if there's a way to test this directly with opencode.\n\nBut first, let me make sure the provider is correctly configured in opencode. The config looks correct, but I need to verify that opencode can actually load and use it.\n\nLet me create a simple test to see if the provider works when called directly.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "tool_RzXYb0HR5Elf2KJa20yDJirQ", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "bash", "arguments": "{\"command\":\"node -e \\\"\\nconst p = require('/Users/alex/.config/opencode/node_modules/@swen3/provider');\\nconst provider = p.createSwen3Provider();\\nconst model = provider.languageModel('swarm');\\n\\n// Test doStream\\nmodel.doStream({ prompt: [{ role: 'user', content: 'Hello' }] }).then(result => {\\n  console.log('Stream created');\\n  const reader = result.stream.getReader();\\n  \\n  function read() {\\n    reader.read().then(({ done, value }) => {\\n      if (done) {\\n        console.log('Stream complete');\\n        return;\\n      }\\n      process.stdout.write(value);\\n      read();\\n    });\\n  }\\n  \\n  read();\\n});\\n\\\"\",\"description\":\"Test streaming\",\"timeout\":30000}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "tool_RzXYb0HR5Elf2KJa20yDJirQ", "content": "[Old tool result content cleared]"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "The provider works! I can see it's trying to connect to the Zenoh mesh. The error about port 7447 being in use is expected since we're running multiple workers simultaneously and they all try to bind to the same port.\n\nLooking at the output, I can see:\n1. The provider correctly streams the \"thinking\" messages\n2. It runs all three workers in parallel\n3. It gets responses from the workers\n4. It shows the completion status\n\nHowever, there's an issue with the Zenoh connection - multiple processes are trying to bind to the same port. This is because each worker process tries to create its own Zenoh listener.\n\nLooking at the error more carefully, I see that `glm_flash` actually succeeded (it shows \"Hello! How can I help you today?\"), while `qwen3_5_4b_opus` and `jetson_gemma4b` failed with port conflicts.\n\nThis is actually a known issue from the discoveries section. Let me check if there's a way to fix this in the Python backend.\n\nActually, looking at the discoveries again:\n> Zenoh имеет ограничение — нельзя создать два listener на одном порту, поэтому каждый процесс должен использовать один и тот же Zenoh session или не слушать\n\nThe solution is to either:\n1. Use a shared Zenoh session\n2. Not listen on a port (connect only)\n\nLet me check the Python code to see how it handles Zenoh connections.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "tool_m3HhPTChOjkepTIba0SL1xfc", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "bash", "arguments": "{\"command\":\"grep -n \\\"zenoh\\\" ~/.local/share/swen3/autonomous_swarm.py | head -20\",\"description\":\"Find zenoh usage in Python\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "tool_m3HhPTChOjkepTIba0SL1xfc", "content": "[Old tool result content cleared]"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "tool_o91vRr9hY7q5TtU5oIStQGAm", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "read", "arguments": "{\"filePath\":\"/Users/alex/.local/share/swen3/autonomous_swarm.py\",\"limit\":50}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "tool_o91vRr9hY7q5TtU5oIStQGAm", "content": "[Old tool result content cleared]"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I see the issue - the Python script is trying to listen on port 7447, which causes conflicts when multiple instances run simultaneously. The solution is to remove the `zenoh_listen` parameter so it only connects (client mode) without binding to a port.\n\nLet me update the Python script to not listen on any port.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "tool_vx0noqqn9LLX1JFiWlXLt7r1", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "edit", "arguments": "{\"filePath\":\"/Users/alex/.local/share/swen3/autonomous_swarm.py\",\"oldString\":\"        cfg = Swen3Config(\\n            zenoh_connect=[\\\"tcp/10.15.64.226:7447\\\", \\\"tcp/10.15.66.12:7447\\\"],\\n            zenoh_listen=[\\\"tcp/0.0.0.0:7447\\\"],\\n            roles=self.available_workers,\\n            deadline_ms=60000,\\n        )\",\"newString\":\"        cfg = Swen3Config(\\n            zenoh_connect=[\\\"tcp/10.15.64.226:7447\\\", \\\"tcp/10.15.66.12:7447\\\"],\\n            roles=self.available_workers,\\n            deadline_ms=60000,\\n        )\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "tool_vx0noqqn9LLX1JFiWlXLt7r1", "content": "[Old tool result content cleared]"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Now let me test the provider again to see if the port conflict is resolved.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "tool_xiwpGH9eeC7BHw6nRLRRsmx4", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "bash", "arguments": "{\"command\":\"node -e \\\"\\nconst p = require('/Users/alex/.config/opencode/node_modules/@swen3/provider');\\nconst provider = p.createSwen3Provider();\\nconst model = provider.languageModel('swarm');\\n\\n// Test doStream with timeout\\nmodel.doStream({ prompt: [{ role: 'user', content: 'Hello' }] }).then(result => {\\n  console.log('Stream created');\\n  const reader = result.stream.getReader();\\n  \\n  function read() {\\n    reader.read().then(({ done, value }) => {\\n      if (done) {\\n        console.log('Stream complete');\\n        return;\\n      }\\n      process.stdout.write(value);\\n      read();\\n    }).catch(err => {\\n      console.error('Read error:', err);\\n    });\\n  }\\n  \\n  read();\\n});\\n\\\" 2>&1 | head -50\",\"description\":\"Test streaming again\",\"timeout\":60000}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "tool_xiwpGH9eeC7BHw6nRLRRsmx4", "content": "[Old tool result content cleared]"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "The port conflict is resolved! Now all three workers can connect successfully. I can see responses from:\n- `glm_flash` - responded with a greeting\n- `qwen3_5_4b_opus` - responded with a more detailed greeting\n- `jetson_gemma4b` - responded as well\n\nThe provider is working correctly. Now I need to make sure opencode can actually use this provider. Let me check if there are any issues with how opencode loads the provider.\n\nLooking at the test output, I notice that the stream is working but it's quite verbose with all the status messages. For opencode integration, I should probably clean up the output to make it more readable.\n\nBut first, let me verify that the provider is properly configured and test if opencode can use it. Let me check if there's a way to test the provider directly with opencode.\n\nActually, I realize I should test if the provider works when opencode tries to use it. The best way to do this is to try running opencode with the provider configured.\n\nBut before that, let me make sure the provider returns data in the format that opencode expects. Looking at the AI SDK interface, the stream should return text chunks, not just any strings.\n\nLet me update the provider to ensure it returns proper text chunks.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "tool_evKqqfFrXKBABH01Jfq9sqvt", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "read", "arguments": "{\"filePath\":\"/Users/alex/.local/share/swen3/provider/src/index.ts\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "tool_evKqqfFrXKBABH01Jfq9sqvt", "content": "[Old tool result content cleared]"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "The provider looks good. Now let me verify that opencode can actually load and use this provider. Let me check if there are any issues with the opencode configuration.\n\nActually, I just realized something - the current setup has the provider configured, but I need to make sure opencode actually tries to use it. Let me check if there's a way to verify the provider is being loaded correctly.\n\nLet me also check if the provider needs to handle the `messages` format differently. Looking at the AI SDK interface, it seems like opencode might pass messages in a different format than what I'm expecting.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "tool_1reEOhbSpgVx5rKggO6atCKk", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "bash", "arguments": "{\"command\":\"cat ~/.local/share/swen3/provider/dist/index.js | head -50\",\"description\":\"Check compiled provider\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "tool_1reEOhbSpgVx5rKggO6atCKk", "content": "[Old tool result content cleared]"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "The compiled provider looks correct. Now let me check if opencode is actually configured to use this provider. Let me verify the config one more time and check if there's a way to test it.\n\nActually, I should check if opencode needs to be restarted to pick up the new provider configuration. But more importantly, I should verify that the provider interface matches what opencode expects.\n\nLooking at the code, I notice that the provider returns a stream of strings, but the AI SDK might expect a specific format for streaming chunks. Let me check if there's a standard format for text deltas in the AI SDK.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "tool_jCOoCpilDm2WRnN966iwlW2f", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "bash", "arguments": "{\"command\":\"cat ~/.local/share/swen3/provider/node_modules/@ai-sdk/provider/dist/index.d.ts | grep -A 20 \\\"LanguageModelV1StreamPart\\\" | head -40\",\"description\":\"Check stream part types\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "tool_jCOoCpilDm2WRnN966iwlW2f", "content": "[Old tool result content cleared]"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Ah, I see! The AI SDK expects the stream to return `LanguageModelV1StreamPart` objects, not just plain strings. The stream parts should have a specific format like `{ type: 'text-delta', textDelta: '...' }`.\n\nLet me update the provider to return the correct format.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "tool_FUbwmLJVrvWU0421iMmPXx7W", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "write", "arguments": "{\"content\":\"import { spawn } from \\\"child_process\\\";\\nimport { ReadableStream } from \\\"stream/web\\\";\\n\\nexport interface Swen3ProviderOptions {\\n  zenohConnect?: string[];\\n  workers?: string[];\\n  timeout?: number;\\n}\\n\\n// System prompt для роя\\nconst SWARM_SYSTEM_PROMPT = `Ты — распределённый рой ИИ-агентов SWEN v3.\\nТы состоишь из нескольких воркеров, которые работают параллельно:\\n- qwen3_5_4b_opus (Diana): сложные задачи, анализ\\n- glm_flash (Diana): код, технические тексты  \\n- jetson_gemma4b (Jetson): простые задачи, факты\\n\\nВсе воркеры получают один и тот же запрос и отвечают независимо.\\nЗатем выбирается лучший ответ.\\n\\nОтвечай на языке запроса пользователя.`;\\n\\n// AI SDK stream part types\\ntype TextDeltaPart = {\\n  type: \\\"text-delta\\\";\\n  textDelta: string;\\n};\\n\\ntype FinishPart = {\\n  type: \\\"finish\\\";\\n  finishReason: \\\"stop\\\" | \\\"length\\\" | \\\"content-filter\\\" | \\\"tool-calls\\\" | \\\"error\\\" | \\\"other\\\";\\n  usage?: {\\n    promptTokens: number;\\n    completionTokens: number;\\n  };\\n};\\n\\ntype StreamPart = TextDeltaPart | FinishPart;\\n\\nclass Swen3LanguageModel {\\n  readonly specificationVersion = \\\"v1\\\" as const;\\n  readonly provider = \\\"swen3\\\";\\n  readonly modelId = \\\"swarm\\\";\\n  readonly defaultObjectGenerationMode = undefined;\\n  readonly supportsImageUrls = false;\\n  readonly supportsStructuredOutputs = false;\\n\\n  private options: Swen3ProviderOptions;\\n\\n  constructor(options: Swen3ProviderOptions = {}) {\\n    this.options = {\\n      zenohConnect: [\\\"tcp/10.15.64.226:7447\\\", \\\"tcp/10.15.66.12:7447\\\"],\\n      workers: [\\\"glm_flash\\\", \\\"qwen3_5_4b_opus\\\", \\\"jetson_gemma4b\\\"],\\n      timeout: 120000,\\n      ...options,\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n  async doGenerate(options: any): Promise<any> {\\n    const stream = await this.doStream(options);\\n    const chunks: string[] = [];\\n    \\n    const reader = stream.stream.getReader();\\n    while (true) {\\n      const { done, value } = await reader.read();\\n      if (done) break;\\n      if (value.type === \\\"text-delta\\\") {\\n        chunks.push(value.textDelta);\\n      }\\n    }\\n\\n    const text = chunks.join(\\\"\\\");\\n    \\n    return {\\n      text,\\n      finishReason: \\\"stop\\\" as const,\\n      usage: {\\n        promptTokens: 0,\\n        completionTokens: Math.ceil(text.length / 4),\\n      },\\n      rawCall: {\\n        rawPrompt: options.prompt,\\n        rawSettings: {},\\n      },\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n  async doStream(options: any): Promise<any> {\\n    const messages = options.prompt || [];\\n    const lastMessage = messages.filter((m: any) => m.role === \\\"user\\\").pop();\\n    const question = lastMessage?.content || \\\"\\\";\\n\\n    const stream = new ReadableStream<StreamPart>({\\n      start: async (controller) => {\\n        try {\\n          controller.enqueue({\\n            type: \\\"text-delta\\\",\\n            textDelta: `🌐 SWEN v3 Swarm Thinking...\\\\n\\\\n`,\\n          });\\n\\n          const workerStreams = this.options.workers!.map((worker) =>\\n            this.streamWorker(worker, question, controller)\\n          );\\n\\n          await Promise.all(workerStreams);\\n\\n          controller.enqueue({\\n            type: \\\"text-delta\\\",\\n            textDelta: `\\\\n✅ Swarm complete\\\\n`,\\n          });\\n          \\n          controller.enqueue({\\n            type: \\\"finish\\\",\\n            finishReason: \\\"stop\\\",\\n            usage: {\\n              promptTokens: 0,\\n              completionTokens: 0,\\n            },\\n          });\\n          \\n          controller.close();\\n        } catch (error) {\\n          controller.error(error);\\n        }\\n      },\\n    });\\n\\n    return {\\n      stream,\\n      rawCall: {\\n        rawPrompt: options.prompt,\\n        rawSettings: {},\\n      },\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n  private async streamWorker(\\n    worker: string,\\n    question: string,\\n    controller: ReadableStreamDefaultController<StreamPart>\\n  ): Promise<void> {\\n    return new Promise((resolve) => {\\n      const venv = `${process.env.HOME}/.venvs/swen3`;\\n      const script = `${process.env.HOME}/.local/share/swen3/autonomous_swarm.py`;\\n      const python = `${venv}/bin/python3`;\\n\\n      controller.enqueue({\\n        type: \\\"text-delta\\\",\\n        textDelta: `\\\\n🤖 [${worker}] thinking...\\\\n`,\\n      });\\n\\n      const proc = spawn(python, [script, question], {\\n        env: {\\n          ...process.env,\\n          VIRTUAL_ENV: venv,\\n          PATH: `${venv}/bin:${process.env.PATH}`,\\n          SWEN_WORKERS: worker,\\n        },\\n      });\\n\\n      proc.stdout.on(\\\"data\\\", (data: Buffer) => {\\n        const text = data.toString();\\n        const lines = text.split(\\\"\\\\n\\\");\\n        for (const line of lines) {\\n          if (line.trim() && !line.startsWith(\\\"[Autonomous Swarm]\\\")) {\\n            controller.enqueue({\\n              type: \\\"text-delta\\\",\\n              textDelta: `  ${line}\\\\n`,\\n            });\\n          }\\n        }\\n      });\\n\\n      proc.stderr.on(\\\"data\\\", (data: Buffer) => {\\n        const text = data.toString();\\n        if (text.includes(\\\"Error\\\")) {\\n          controller.enqueue({\\n            type: \\\"text-delta\\\",\\n            textDelta: `  ❌ Error: ${text.trim()}\\\\n`,\\n          });\\n        }\\n      });\\n\\n      proc.on(\\\"close\\\", (code) => {\\n        try {\\n          if (code === 0) {\\n            controller.enqueue({\\n              type: \\\"text-delta\\\",\\n              textDelta: `  ✅ [${worker}] done\\\\n`,\\n            });\\n          } else {\\n            controller.enqueue({\\n              type: \\\"text-delta\\\",\\n              textDelta: `  ❌ [${worker}] failed (code ${code})\\\\n`,\\n            });\\n          }\\n        } catch (e) {\\n          // Controller already closed, ignore\\n        }\\n        resolve();\\n      });\\n\\n      proc.on(\\\"error\\\", (err) => {\\n        try {\\n          controller.enqueue({\\n            type: \\\"text-delta\\\",\\n            textDelta: `  ❌ [${worker}] error: ${err.message}\\\\n`,\\n          });\\n        } catch (e) {\\n          // Controller already closed, ignore\\n        }\\n        resolve();\\n      });\\n\\n      setTimeout(() => {\\n        proc.kill();\\n        try {\\n          controller.enqueue({\\n            type: \\\"text-delta\\\",\\n            textDelta: `  ⏱️ [${worker}] timeout\\\\n`,\\n          });\\n        } catch (e) {\\n          // Controller already closed, ignore\\n        }\\n        resolve();\\n      }, this.options.timeout);\\n    });\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n// Provider factory\\nexport class Swen3Provider {\\n  private options: Swen3ProviderOptions;\\n\\n  constructor(options: Swen3ProviderOptions = {}) {\\n    this.options = options;\\n  }\\n\\n  languageModel(modelId: string): Swen3LanguageModel {\\n    return new Swen3LanguageModel(this.options);\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n// Factory function for AI SDK compatibility\\nexport function createSwen3Provider(options?: Swen3ProviderOptions): Swen3Provider {\\n  return new Swen3Provider(options);\\n}\\n\\n// Default export\\nexport default createSwen3Provider;\\n\",\"filePath\":\"/Users/alex/.local/share/swen3/provider/src/index.ts\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "tool_FUbwmLJVrvWU0421iMmPXx7W", "content": "[Old tool result content cleared]"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "tool_W5EOkUFu5Eqt4Q7DGe9EqzkZ", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "bash", "arguments": "{\"command\":\"cd ~/.local/share/swen3/provider && npm run build\",\"description\":\"Rebuild provider with proper format\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "tool_W5EOkUFu5Eqt4Q7DGe9EqzkZ", "content": "[Old tool result content cleared]"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "tool_l7hSzJSTOXl4lkz3LCFDKhWb", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "bash", "arguments": "{\"command\":\"node -e \\\"\\nconst p = require('/Users/alex/.config/opencode/node_modules/@swen3/provider');\\nconst provider = p.createSwen3Provider();\\nconst model = provider.languageModel('swarm');\\n\\n// Test doStream\\nmodel.doStream({ prompt: [{ role: 'user', content: 'Hello' }] }).then(result => {\\n  console.log('Stream created');\\n  const reader = result.stream.getReader();\\n  \\n  function read() {\\n    reader.read().then(({ done, value }) => {\\n      if (done) {\\n        console.log('Stream complete');\\n        return;\\n      }\\n      if (value.type === 'text-delta') {\\n        process.stdout.write(value.textDelta);\\n      }\\n      read();\\n    });\\n  }\\n  \\n  read();\\n});\\n\\\" 2>&1 | head -30\",\"description\":\"Test formatted streaming\",\"timeout\":60000}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "tool_l7hSzJSTOXl4lkz3LCFDKhWb", "content": "[Old tool result content cleared]"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "The provider is working correctly with the proper AI SDK format. Now I need to make sure opencode can actually use this provider. Let me verify the configuration is correct and test if opencode picks it up.\n\nLooking at the current state:\n1. ✅ Provider implements AI SDK interface\n2. ✅ Provider is built and linked\n3. ✅ Config has `model: \"swen3/swarm\"` set\n4. ✅ Python backend connects without port conflicts\n\nNow I should test if opencode actually uses this provider. However, I realize there might be an issue - the current setup still uses the agent + tool approach (`swen3_ask`), but the goal is to make opencode use the SWEN v3 provider directly as the LLM backend.\n\nLet me check if opencode is currently running and if I can test the provider integration.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "tool_AODjU3tJhONh7RAVQ1HmaQzk", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "bash", "arguments": "{\"command\":\"ps aux | grep opencode | grep -v grep || echo \\\"opencode not running\\\"\",\"description\":\"Check if opencode is running\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "tool_AODjU3tJhONh7RAVQ1HmaQzk", "content": "[Old tool result content cleared]"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Opencode is running. Now I need to check if the provider is properly loaded. Let me verify the current configuration and see if there are any issues.\n\nActually, looking at the process list, I see opencode is running. But I need to make sure it's using the correct configuration. Let me check if there's a way to verify which model/provider opencode is currently using.\n\nLet me also check if the provider needs to be reloaded. Since opencode might cache the provider, I should check if there's a way to reload it.\n\nBut first, let me verify that the configuration is correct by checking the opencode.json file one more time.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "tool_G4JTl30HKMZoVouGprHUDNsn", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "read", "arguments": "{\"filePath\":\"/Users/alex/.config/opencode/opencode.json\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "tool_G4JTl30HKMZoVouGprHUDNsn", "content": "[Old tool result content cleared]"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "The configuration looks correct. I see that:\n1. `model` is set to `\"swen3/swarm\"` \n2. `small_model` is also set to `\"swen3/swarm\"`\n3. The `swen3` provider is configured with the correct npm package\n\nHowever, I notice there's no `default_agent` set. Looking at the agents section, I see several agents including `autonomous-swarm` which is marked as `mode: primary`. \n\nBut wait - I need to understand how opencode works. When opencode starts, it uses the default agent (which is \"build\" if not specified) and the configured model. The agent then decides how to process the user's request.\n\nLooking at the current setup, the `autonomous-swarm` agent is configured to use `swen3_ask` tool, but the goal is to make opencode use the SWEN v3 provider directly as the LLM backend, bypassing the local LLM entirely.\n\nLet me check if there's a way to make opencode use the provider directly without going through an agent. Looking at the docs, it seems like the `model` field should make opencode use that model directly.\n\nBut I think the issue is that opencode might still be using a local LLM for the agent's reasoning, and only using the provider for the final response. To achieve true \"no LLM on opencode side\", I need to make sure the agent itself uses the SWEN v3 provider.\n\nLet me update the agent configuration to use the `swen3/swarm` model explicitly.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "tool_eHZI0EX7lnjN70HOULbvP5zJ", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "read", "arguments": "{\"filePath\":\"/Users/alex/.config/opencode/agents/autonomous-swarm.md\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "tool_eHZI0EX7lnjN70HOULbvP5zJ", "content": "[Old tool result content cleared]"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I see the issue now. The current `autonomous-swarm` agent is designed to use the `swen3_ask` tool, which means it's still using opencode's local LLM to decide when to call the tool. This is not true \"no LLM on opencode side\".\n\nTo achieve the goal of making opencode use SWEN v3 directly as the LLM backend, I need to:\n\n1. Set the `autonomous-swarm` agent to use the `swen3/swarm` model directly\n2. OR, make the default agent use the SWEN v3 provider\n\nLooking at the opencode docs, I can set a `model` field in the agent configuration to specify which model it should use. Let me update the agent configuration.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "tool_K7VA23hq5aqoFdQg4F7kuK2A", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "edit", "arguments": "{\"filePath\":\"/Users/alex/.config/opencode/agents/autonomous-swarm.md\",\"oldString\":\"---\\ndescription: >\\n  Autonomous Swarm — полностью автономный рой ИИ-агентов.\\n  НЕТ принятия решений на стороне opencode — ВСЁ делегируется воркерам роя.\\n  Простой passthrough агент: получает запрос → отправляет в рой → возвращает ответ.\\n  \\n  Рой сам решает:\\n  - Как декомпозировать задачу\\n  - Какие воркеры использовать\\n  - Как оценивать результаты\\n  - Какой ответ выбрать\\nmode: primary\\npermission:\\n  edit: allow\\n  bash: allow\\n  read: allow\\n  glob: allow\\n  grep: allow\\n  swen3_ask: allow\\n  swen3_status: allow\\n---\",\"newString\":\"---\\ndescription: >\\n  Autonomous Swarm — полностью автономный рой ИИ-агентов.\\n  НЕТ принятия решений на стороне opencode — ВСЁ делегируется воркерам роя.\\n  Простой passthrough агент: получает запрос → отправляет в рой → возвращает ответ.\\n  \\n  Рой сам решает:\\n  - Как декомпозировать задачу\\n  - Какие воркеры использовать\\n  - Как оценивать результаты\\n  - Какой ответ выбрать\\nmode: primary\\nmodel: swen3/swarm\\npermission:\\n  edit: allow\\n  bash: allow\\n  read: allow\\n  glob: allow\\n  grep: allow\\n  swen3_ask: allow\\n  swen3_status: allow\\n---\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "tool_K7VA23hq5aqoFdQg4F7kuK2A", "content": "[Old tool result content cleared]"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Now I need to set this as the default agent so opencode uses it automatically. Let me update the opencode.json to set the default agent.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "tool_0jSyISySNlBElT70sogiLuNM", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "edit", "arguments": "{\"filePath\":\"/Users/alex/.config/opencode/opencode.json\",\"oldString\":\"  \\\"$schema\\\": \\\"https://opencode.ai/config.json\\\",\\n  \\\"model\\\": \\\"swen3/swarm\\\",\\n  \\\"small_model\\\": \\\"swen3/swarm\\\",\",\"newString\":\"  \\\"$schema\\\": \\\"https://opencode.ai/config.json\\\",\\n  \\\"model\\\": \\\"swen3/swarm\\\",\\n  \\\"small_model\\\": \\\"swen3/swarm\\\",\\n  \\\"default_agent\\\": \\\"autonomous-swarm\\\",\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "tool_0jSyISySNlBElT70sogiLuNM", "content": "[Old tool result content cleared]"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Now let me verify the configuration is valid and summarize what we've accomplished.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "tool_1mT7zPzPmFQtfLNXNr40KYVr", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "bash", "arguments": "{\"command\":\"python3 -m json.tool ~/.config/opencode/opencode.json > /dev/null && echo \\\"✅ Valid JSON\\\" || echo \\\"❌ Invalid JSON\\\"\",\"description\":\"Validate config\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "tool_1mT7zPzPmFQtfLNXNr40KYVr", "content": "[Old tool result content cleared]"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "tool_4fxcx8JKlchD39anYE4wZTsX", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "bash", "arguments": "{\"command\":\"cat ~/.config/opencode/opencode.json | grep -E \\\"(model|default_agent)\\\" | head -5\",\"description\":\"Check key config values\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "tool_4fxcx8JKlchD39anYE4wZTsX", "content": "[Old tool result content cleared]"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "The configuration is set up correctly. Now let me create a summary of what we've accomplished and what the next steps should be.\n\n## Summary\n\nWe've successfully set up the SWEN v3 provider to work with opencode. Here's what was accomplished:\n\n### ✅ Completed:\n\n1. **Provider Implementation**: Created `@swen3/provider` package that implements the AI SDK `LanguageModelV1` interface\n2. **Streaming Support**: Provider supports streaming responses from all workers in parallel\n3. **Port Conflict Fix**: Removed `zenoh_listen` from Python backend to avoid port binding conflicts\n4. **Configuration**: Set `model` and `small_model` to `\"swen3/swarm\"` in `opencode.json`\n5. **Default Agent**: Set `default_agent` to `\"autonomous-swarm\"` \n6. **Agent Model**: Updated `autonomous-swarm` agent to use `model: swen3/swarm`\n\n### 🔧 How it works:\n\n1. When opencode starts, it loads the `autonomous-swarm` agent\n2. The agent is configured to use the `swen3/swarm` model\n3. Opencode loads the `@swen3/provider` package\n4. When the user sends a message, opencode calls the provider's `doStream()` or `doGenerate()`\n5. The provider spawns Python processes for each worker in parallel\n6. Each worker connects to the Zenoh mesh and gets a response\n7. The provider streams all responses back to opencode\n\n### 📝 Next Steps / Testing:\n\nTo verify everything works:\n1. Restart opencode to pick up the new configuration\n2. Send a test message like \"Hello\" \n3. You should see the SWEN v3 swarm thinking output with all workers responding\n\n### ⚠️ Known Issues:\n- The output is quite verbose with status messages from all workers\n- Worker responses are shown sequentially, not truly merged\n- No actual \"judging\" or selection of best response happens in the provider\n\nWould you like me to:\n1. Test the integration by restarting opencode?\n2. Clean up the output format to be more concise?\n3. Add actual response synthesis/selection logic?"}, {"role": "user", "content": "как дела?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Ответ роя: \"как дела?\"", "tool_calls": [{"id": "tool_4HZClRbck0BI6Xs8rmEiOtbp", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "swen3_ask", "arguments": "{\"question\":\"как дела?\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "tool_4HZClRbck0BI6Xs8rmEiOtbp", "content": "[Old tool result content cleared]"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Рой работает! Все 3 воркера ответили, и судья выбрал ответ от `jetson_gemma4b` (быстрейший — 20 сек).\n\n**Что произошло:**\n- `qwen3_5_4b_opus` — 12.1с\n- `jetson_gemma4b` — 20.1с ⭐ (выбран победителем)\n- `glm_flash` — 25.7с\n\n**Статус интеграции:**\n- ✅ Рой отвечает на запросы\n- ✅ Параллельный fanout работает\n- ✅ Судейство выбирает лучший ответ\n- ⚠️ Провайдер для opencode настроен, но opencode пока использует `swen3_ask` tool вместо прямого вызова провайдера\n\n**Что дальше?**\n1. Перезапустить opencode, чтобы он начал использовать `swen3/swarm` как LLM backend\n2. Или оставить текущий workflow с `swen3_ask` tool (тоже рабочий вариант)\n\nКакой вариант предпочитаешь?"}, {"role": "user", "content": "как дела?"}, {"role": "user", "content": "как дела?"}, {"role": "user", "content": "провайдет не запускается"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Провайдер не запускается? Давай диагностируем.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "tool_WpAFd7bCho7mdOU0bMZMIP6X", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "bash", "arguments": "{\"command\":\"node -e \\\"\\nconst p = require('/Users/alex/.config/opencode/node_modules/@swen3/provider');\\nconsole.log('Provider loaded:', typeof p);\\nconsole.log('createSwen3Provider:', typeof p.createSwen3Provider);\\nconst provider = p.createSwen3Provider();\\nconsole.log('languageModel:', typeof provider.languageModel);\\nconst model = provider.languageModel('swarm');\\nconsole.log('specificationVersion:', model.specificationVersion);\\nconsole.log('doStream:', typeof model.doStream);\\nconsole.log('doGenerate:', typeof model.doGenerate);\\n\\\" 2>&1\",\"description\":\"Test provider loading\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "tool_WpAFd7bCho7mdOU0bMZMIP6X", "content": "[Old tool result content cleared]"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Провайдер загружается нормально. Проблема может быть в:\n\n1. **Opencode не видит провайдер** — проверим symlink\n2. **Opencode не подхватывает конфиг** — нужен рестарт\n3. **Opencode использует другой model** — проверим текущий model\n\nДавай проверим:", "tool_calls": [{"id": "tool_PAWsP6gX6D8oZks0Y0cbEaHl", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "bash", "arguments": "{\"command\":\"ls -la ~/.config/opencode/node_modules/@swen3/ 2>/dev/null || echo \\\"No @swen3 directory\\\"\",\"description\":\"Check provider symlink\"}"}}, {"id": "tool_hAQhccCv8sM7ctrpu2ycilNT", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "bash", "arguments": "{\"command\":\"cat ~/.config/opencode/opencode.json | grep -A 2 '\\\"model\\\"'\",\"description\":\"Check current model\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "tool_PAWsP6gX6D8oZks0Y0cbEaHl", "content": "[Old tool result content cleared]"}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "tool_hAQhccCv8sM7ctrpu2ycilNT", "content": "[Old tool result content cleared]"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Symlink на месте, конфиг правильный. Проблема в том, что **opencode запущен до изменений** и кэшировал старый провайдер.\n\n**Решение:** Нужно перезапустить opencode, чтобы он подхватил новый провайдер.\n\nВыполни в терминале:\n```bash\n# Найди PID opencode и убей процесс\nkill $(pgrep -f \"opencode\")\n\n# Или если запущен в фоне\npkill -f opencode\n\n# Затем запусти заново\nopencode\n```\n\nПосле перезапуска opencode должен:\n1. Загрузить `@swen3/provider` из `node_modules`\n2. Использовать `swen3/swarm` как модель по умолчанию\n3. При запросе вызывать `doStream()` у провайдера вместо локального LLM\n\n**Проверка после рестарта:**\nОтправь сообщение — должно появиться:\n```\n🌐 SWEN v3 Swarm Thinking...\n\n🤖 [glm_flash] thinking...\n🤖 [qwen3_5_4b_opus] thinking...  \n🤖 [jetson_gemma4b] thinking...\n```\n\nПерезапусти opencode и проверь!"}, {"role": "user", "content": "как дела?"}, {"role": "user", "content": "пишет  ProviderInitError"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "ProviderInitError — провайдер не инициализируется. Давай найдём причину.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "tool_QPrXq3fzHvWhOFXXeSqDNpVI", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "bash", "arguments": "{\"command\":\"node -e \\\"\\ntry {\\n  const p = require('/Users/alex/.config/opencode/node_modules/@swen3/provider');\\n  console.log('✅ Provider loaded');\\n  const provider = p.createSwen3Provider();\\n  console.log('✅ Provider created');\\n  const model = provider.languageModel('swarm');\\n  console.log('✅ Model created');\\n  console.log('Model props:', Object.keys(model));\\n} catch (e) {\\n  console.error('❌ Error:', e.message);\\n  console.error(e.stack);\\n}\\n\\\" 2>&1\",\"description\":\"Debug provider init\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "tool_QPrXq3fzHvWhOFXXeSqDNpVI", "content": "[Old tool result content cleared]"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Провайдер загружается нормально вручную. Значит проблема в том, как opencode его инициализирует. Давай проверим:\n\n1. **Есть ли package.json у провайдера?**\n2. **Правильно ли указан main в package.json?**\n3. **Может opencode ожидает другой формат экспорта?**", "tool_calls": [{"id": "tool_KhTURWuQT3punoTQfB07MqRN", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "bash", "arguments": "{\"command\":\"cat ~/.local/share/swen3/provider/package.json\",\"description\":\"Check provider package.json\"}"}}, {"id": "tool_WmfCh9LQ85eUgBo4HS1nqY6q", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "bash", "arguments": "{\"command\":\"cat ~/.local/share/swen3/provider/dist/index.js | head -20\",\"description\":\"Check compiled output\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "tool_KhTURWuQT3punoTQfB07MqRN", "content": "[Old tool result content cleared]"}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "tool_WmfCh9LQ85eUgBo4HS1nqY6q", "content": "[Old tool result content cleared]"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Вижу проблему! `\"type\": \"module\"` в package.json, но opencode использует CommonJS (`require`). Проверим:", "tool_calls": [{"id": "tool_xEubkkOBdBtVTaeuCJbvI5T0", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "bash", "arguments": "{\"command\":\"node -e \\\"const p = require('/Users/alex/.config/opencode/node_modules/@swen3/provider'); console.log(p);\\\" 2>&1\",\"description\":\"Test CommonJS require\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "tool_xEubkkOBdBtVTaeuCJbvI5T0", "content": "[Old tool result content cleared]"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Require работает (Node поддерживает ESM через require). Значит проблема не в этом.\n\nДавай проверим, что именно пишет opencode. Может быть проблема в опциях?", "tool_calls": [{"id": "tool_CUczt6BMyl5PAZ50NSedoHtl", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "bash", "arguments": "{\"command\":\"node -e \\\"\\nconst p = require('/Users/alex/.config/opencode/node_modules/@swen3/provider');\\nconst provider = p.createSwen3Provider({\\n  zenohConnect: ['tcp/10.15.64.226:7447', 'tcp/10.15.66.12:7447'],\\n  workers: ['glm_flash', 'qwen3_5_4b_opus', 'jetson_gemma4b']\\n});\\nconst model = provider.languageModel('swarm');\\nconsole.log('✅ Provider with options works');\\n\\\" 2>&1\",\"description\":\"Test provider with options\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "tool_CUczt6BMyl5PAZ50NSedoHtl", "content": "[Old tool result content cleared]"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Провайдер работает с опциями. Значит opencode падает при инициализации. Давай посмотрим логи opencode:", "tool_calls": [{"id": "tool_xofkfhIruykXJeip7hJDBzsp", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "bash", "arguments": "{\"command\":\"ls -la ~/.local/share/opencode/logs/ 2>/dev/null || ls -la ~/.config/opencode/logs/ 2>/dev/null || echo \\\"No logs directory found\\\"\",\"description\":\"Find opencode logs\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "tool_xofkfhIruykXJeip7hJDBzsp", "content": "[Old tool result content cleared]"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "tool_TITRw4oqA3y4xL9ImKhB2ZVb", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "bash", "arguments": "{\"command\":\"find ~/.local/share/opencode -name \\\"*.log\\\" 2>/dev/null | head -5\",\"description\":\"Search for log files\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "tool_TITRw4oqA3y4xL9ImKhB2ZVb", "content": "[Old tool result content cleared]"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "tool_57Xmyo3lnGEufkHlQA2nyWFJ", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "bash", "arguments": "{\"command\":\"ls -lt ~/.local/share/opencode/log/ | head -5\",\"description\":\"List recent logs\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "tool_57Xmyo3lnGEufkHlQA2nyWFJ", "content": "[Old tool result content cleared]"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "tool_gVmFarMI5Lq54DTMb4efxw3F", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "bash", "arguments": "{\"command\":\"grep -i \\\"error\\\\|providerinit\\\\|swen3\\\" ~/.local/share/opencode/log/2026-04-29T143720.log | tail -20\",\"description\":\"Check recent logs for errors\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "tool_gVmFarMI5Lq54DTMb4efxw3F", "content": "[Old tool result content cleared]"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Логи показывают, что opencode использует `swen3_ask` tool, а не провайдер напрямую. Значит opencode не загружает наш провайдер как LLM backend.\n\nДавай проверим, что opencode видит в конфиге:", "tool_calls": [{"id": "tool_NJ4ZQRPbQYAfYV3u9ziivxrZ", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "bash", "arguments": "{\"command\":\"grep -i \\\"providerinit\\\\|error.*swen3\\\\|failed.*provider\\\" ~/.local/share/opencode/log/2026-04-29T143720.log | head -20\",\"description\":\"Search for provider errors\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "tool_NJ4ZQRPbQYAfYV3u9ziivxrZ", "content": "[Old tool result content cleared]"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Нашёл! В логе:\n\n```\nERROR 2026-04-29T14:37:52 +1ms service=session.processor ... error=ProviderInitError stack=ProviderInitError: ProviderInitError\n```\n\nПровайдер падает при инициализации. Давай посмотрим полный stack trace:", "tool_calls": [{"id": "tool_7mqM600J7eF4zX4f0Ldns5ML", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "bash", "arguments": "{\"command\":\"grep -A 20 \\\"ProviderInitError\\\" ~/.local/share/opencode/log/2026-04-29T143720.log | head -30\",\"description\":\"Get full error stack\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "tool_7mqM600J7eF4zX4f0Ldns5ML", "content": "[Old tool result content cleared]"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Stack trace обрезан. Проблема в том, что opencode использует Bun runtime, а не Node.js. Провайдер может не работать с Bun.\n\nДавай проверим, есть ли проблемы с ESM/CommonJS в Bun:", "tool_calls": [{"id": "tool_PFXPcFlM2o5u4HLf0AOIvWh0", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "bash", "arguments": "{\"command\":\"bun -e \\\"const p = require('/Users/alex/.config/opencode/node_modules/@swen3/provider'); console.log(p);\\\" 2>&1 || echo \\\"Bun not available\\\"\",\"description\":\"Test with Bun\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "tool_PFXPcFlM2o5u4HLf0AOIvWh0", "content": "[Old tool result content cleared]"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Bun нет в PATH. Давай найдём, где Bun у opencode:", "tool_calls": [{"id": "tool_DlIgcfyDALp9NQbi8ZIHhe0m", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "bash", "arguments": "{\"command\":\"find /opt/homebrew -name \\\"bun\\\" -type f 2>/dev/null | head -3\",\"description\":\"Find bun binary\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "tool_DlIgcfyDALp9NQbi8ZIHhe0m", "content": "[Old tool result content cleared]"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "tool_nhKER9vQWfISVScGIje6Nehw", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "bash", "arguments": "{\"command\":\"ls -la /opt/homebrew/Cellar/opencode/1.4.10/libexec/lib/node_modules/opencode-ai/node_modules/opencode-darwin-arm64/bin/\",\"description\":\"Check opencode bin directory\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "tool_nhKER9vQWfISVScGIje6Nehw", "content": "[Old tool result content cleared]"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Opencode скомпилирован в бинарник (не использует Bun напрямую). Значит проблема в другом.\n\nДавай проверим, может opencode ожидает, что провайдер экспортирует функцию `provider` или что-то подобное? Проверим документацию opencode по кастомным провайдерам.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "tool_MvmmkA9TwSMv21Kn0iTvDYGh", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "webfetch", "arguments": "{\"url\":\"https://opencode.ai/docs/providers/custom-provider\",\"format\":\"text\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "tool_MvmmkA9TwSMv21Kn0iTvDYGh", "content": "StatusCode: non 2xx status code (404 GET https://opencode.ai/docs/providers/custom-provider)"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "tool_TKH1adUz965sUn0SwrpfMb4q", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "webfetch", "arguments": "{\"url\":\"https://opencode.ai/docs/providers\",\"format\":\"text\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "tool_TKH1adUz965sUn0SwrpfMb4q", "content": "[Old tool result content cleared]"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Смотри, в документации написано:\n\n> npm: AI SDK package to use, @ai-sdk/openai-compatible for OpenAI-compatible providers\n\nOpencode ожидает, что `npm` указывает на **AI SDK package**, а не на произвольный пакет. Наш провайдер не является AI SDK пакетом в строгом смысле.\n\n**Проблема:** Opencode пытается загрузить `@swen3/provider` как AI SDK пакет, но он не соответствует ожидаемому интерфейсу.\n\n**Решение:** Нужно либо:\n1. Сделать провайдер совместимым с AI SDK v3 (сложно)\n2. Использовать `@ai-sdk/openai-compatible` как обёртку и проксировать запросы на наш провайдер\n3. Оставить текущий workflow с `swen3_ask` tool (рабочий вариант)\n\nПредлагаю **вариант 2** — создать простой HTTP сервер, который будет проксировать OpenAI-compatible API запросы на наш SWEN3 рой. Тогда opencode сможет использовать `@ai-sdk/openai-compatible` для подключения.\n\nИли **вариант 3** — оставить как есть, потому что `swen3_ask` tool прекрасно работает и делает то же самое.\n\nКакой вариант выбираешь?"}, {"role": "user", "content": "у меня вопрос: можно ли сделать провайдера как lm studio, ведь там не нужны сложные пакеты? я бы хотел чтобы каждая нода роя могла работать входной точкой провайдера роевой модели. это возможно ?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Отличный вопрос! Да, это возможно. Давай разберёмся как.\n\n## Анализ\n\n**LM Studio** работает как **OpenAI-compatible HTTP сервер** (`http://localhost:1234/v1`). Opencode подключается к нему через `@ai-sdk/openai-compatible`, который ожидает стандартный `/v1/chat/completions` endpoint.\n\n**Твоя идея** — сделать каждую ноду роя входной точкой. Это значит:\n- Каждый воркер (Diana, Jetson) запускает **HTTP сервер** с OpenAI-compatible API\n- Opencode подключается к ним как к обычным провайдерам\n- Но при этом они проксируют запросы в **роевой механизм** (fanout + judging)\n\n## Возможные архитектуры\n\n### Вариант A: \"LM Studio для роя\" (централизованный)\nОдна нода (например, Diana) запускает HTTP сервер, который:\n1. Принимает `/v1/chat/completions` запрос\n2. Делает fanout на все воркеры через Zenoh\n3. Возвращает лучший ответ в OpenAI format\n\n**Плюсы:** Простая настройка opencode — один endpoint\n**Минусы:** Single point of failure, нагрузка на одну ноду\n\n### Вариант B: \"Распределённый провайдер\" (твоя идея)\nКаждая нода запускает HTTP сервер, который:\n1. Принимает запросы\n2. Либо отвечает сам (если это его специализация)\n3. Либо делегирует другим нодам через Zenoh\n\n**Плюсы:** Нет центральной точки отказа, load balancing\n**Минусы:** Сложнее в реализации, opencode должен знать о всех нодах\n\n### Вариант C: \"Гибрид\" (рекомендую)\nDiana запускает **роевой gateway** (HTTP сервер), который:\n- Принимает запросы от opencode\n- Распределяет на воркеры (Diana + Jetson)\n- Возвращает потоковый ответ с \"мышлением\" всех воркеров\n\n**Плюсы:** \n- Opencode видит один endpoint (как LM Studio)\n- Рой работает полностью автономно\n- Можно добавить UI для мониторинга\n\n## Техническая реализация\n\nДля OpenAI-compatible API нужно реализовать:\n\n```python\n# Псевдокод\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel\n\napp = FastAPI()\n\nclass ChatRequest(BaseModel):\n    model: str  # \"swarm\" или имя воркера\n    messages: list\n    stream: bool = False\n\n@app.post(\"/v1/chat/completions\")\nasync def chat_completions(request: ChatRequest):\n    if request.model == \"swarm\":\n        # Fanout на всех воркеров\n        results = await swarm.ask_all(request.messages)\n        best = judge.select_best(results)\n        return openai_format(best)\n    else:\n        # Прямой запрос к конкретному воркеру\n        result = await swarm.ask_one(request.model, request.messages)\n        return openai_format(result)\n```\n\n## Вопросы к тебе\n\n1. **Какой вариант** тебе ближе — A, B или C?\n2. **Где запускать gateway** — на Diana (Windows), Jetson, или на MacBook?\n3. **Нужен ли потоковый вывод** \"мышления\" всех воркеров, или достаточно финального ответа?\n\nЭто определит детали реализации."}, {"role": "user", "content": "давай сначала сделаем одну отдельную точку входа openai http server в рой на макбуке, протестим ее и потом уже будем думать как ее имплиментировать во все ноды роя"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Отличный план! Создадим OpenAI-compatible HTTP сервер на MacBook, который будет входной точкой в рой.\n\n## Архитектура\n\n```\nOpencode (MacBook)\n    ↓ HTTP POST /v1/chat/completions\nOpenAI-compatible Server (MacBook, Python/FastAPI)\n    ↓ Zenoh P2P\n    ├─→ glm_flash (Diana)\n    ├─→ qwen3_5_4b_opus (Diana)  \n    └─→ jetson_gemma4b (Jetson)\n    ↓\nJudge выбирает лучший ответ\n    ↓\nOpenAI format response → Opencode\n```\n\n## Шаги\n\n1. Создать FastAPI сервер с `/v1/chat/completions`\n2. Реализовать fanout через существующий Zenoh mesh\n3. Добавить judging/selection\n4. Вернуть ответ в OpenAI format\n5. Протестировать с opencode через `@ai-sdk/openai-compatible`\n\n## Преимущества\n\n- Opencode думает, что это обычный LLM API (как LM Studio)\n- Не нужен кастомный провайдер\n- Работает с любым OpenAI-compatible клиентом\n- Можно смотреть \"мышление\" воркеров в логах сервера\n\nНачинаю реализацию?", "tool_calls": [{"id": "tool_9ryPCw8lmNcurPHh4qo0eOLO", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "todowrite", "arguments": "{\"todos\":[{\"content\":\"Создать FastAPI сервер с OpenAI-compatible API\",\"status\":\"in_progress\",\"priority\":\"high\"},{\"content\":\"Реализовать fanout на воркеров через Zenoh\",\"status\":\"pending\",\"priority\":\"high\"},{\"content\":\"Добавить judging/selection лучшего ответа\",\"status\":\"pending\",\"priority\":\"high\"},{\"content\":\"Настроить opencode с @ai-sdk/openai-compatible\",\"status\":\"pending\",\"priority\":\"high\"},{\"content\":\"Протестировать end-to-end\",\"status\":\"pending\",\"priority\":\"high\"}]}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "tool_9ryPCw8lmNcurPHh4qo0eOLO", "content": "[Old tool result content cleared]"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "tool_8EBbxFimkUcHyKOp87n1KjMF", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "write", "arguments": "{\"content\":\"#!/usr/bin/env python3\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nSWEN v3 OpenAI-compatible API Gateway\\nВходная точка в рой через HTTP API\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nimport asyncio\\nimport json\\nimport os\\nimport sys\\nimport time\\nimport uuid\\nfrom typing import AsyncGenerator, Dict, List, Optional\\n\\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI, HTTPException, Request\\nfrom fastapi.responses import StreamingResponse, JSONResponse\\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel, Field\\nimport uvicorn\\n\\nsys.path.insert(0, os.path.expanduser(\\\"~/.local/share/swen3\\\"))\\nfrom agent import Swen3Agent, Swen3Config\\n\\napp = FastAPI(title=\\\"SWEN v3 Swarm API\\\", version=\\\"1.0.0\\\")\\n\\n# Глобальный агент для связи с роем\\nswarm_agent: Optional[Swen3Agent] = None\\nAVAILABLE_WORKERS = [\\\"glm_flash\\\", \\\"qwen3_5_4b_opus\\\", \\\"jetson_gemma4b\\\"]\\n\\n\\nclass ChatMessage(BaseModel):\\n    role: str\\n    content: str\\n\\n\\nclass ChatCompletionRequest(BaseModel):\\n    model: str = \\\"swarm\\\"\\n    messages: List[ChatMessage]\\n    temperature: Optional[float] = 0.7\\n    max_tokens: Optional[int] = None\\n    stream: bool = False\\n    # Дополнительные поля для совместимости\\n    top_p: Optional[float] = None\\n    frequency_penalty: Optional[float] = None\\n    presence_penalty: Optional[float] = None\\n\\n\\nclass ChatCompletionChoice(BaseModel):\\n    index: int\\n    message: Optional[Dict] = None\\n    delta: Optional[Dict] = None\\n    finish_reason: Optional[str] = None\\n\\n\\nclass ChatCompletionResponse(BaseModel):\\n    id: str\\n    object: str = \\\"chat.completion\\\"\\n    created: int\\n    model: str\\n    choices: List[ChatCompletionChoice]\\n    usage: Dict = Field(default_factory=dict)\\n\\n\\nasync def connect_swarm():\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Подключение к Zenoh mesh\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    global swarm_agent\\n    cfg = Swen3Config(\\n        zenoh_connect=[\\\"tcp/10.15.64.226:7447\\\", \\\"tcp/10.15.66.12:7447\\\"],\\n        roles=AVAILABLE_WORKERS,\\n        deadline_ms=120000,\\n    )\\n    swarm_agent = Swen3Agent(cfg)\\n    if not swarm_agent.connect():\\n        raise Exception(f\\\"Cannot connect to swarm: {swarm_agent.status}\\\")\\n    await asyncio.sleep(1)\\n    print(\\\"✅ Connected to SWEN v3 swarm\\\")\\n\\n\\ndef extract_last_message(messages: List[ChatMessage]) -> str:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Извлекает последнее user сообщение\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    for msg in reversed(messages):\\n        if msg.role == \\\"user\\\":\\n            return msg.content\\n    return \\\"\\\"\\n\\n\\nasync def ask_worker(worker: str, question: str) -> Dict:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Запрос к одному воркеру\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    try:\\n        result = swarm_agent.ask_one(worker, question, f\\\"api-{time.time()}\\\")\\n        if result.ok:\\n            return {\\n                \\\"worker\\\": worker,\\n                \\\"answer\\\": result.answer,\\n                \\\"latency_ms\\\": result.latency_ms,\\n                \\\"status\\\": \\\"success\\\"\\n            }\\n        else:\\n            return {\\n                \\\"worker\\\": worker,\\n                \\\"answer\\\": \\\"\\\",\\n                \\\"error\\\": result.error,\\n                \\\"status\\\": \\\"error\\\"\\n            }\\n    except Exception as e:\\n        return {\\n            \\\"worker\\\": worker,\\n            \\\"answer\\\": \\\"\\\",\\n            \\\"error\\\": str(e),\\n            \\\"status\\\": \\\"error\\\"\\n        }\\n\\n\\ndef judge_best_response(results: List[Dict]) -> Optional[Dict]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Выбирает лучший ответ из всех воркеров\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    successful = [r for r in results if r[\\\"status\\\"] == \\\"success\\\" and r[\\\"answer\\\"]]\\n    \\n    if not successful:\\n        return None\\n    \\n    # Простая эвристика: выбираем ответ с наибольшей длиной и успешным статусом\\n    # В будущем можно добавить LLM-based judging\\n    best = max(successful, key=lambda x: len(x[\\\"answer\\\"]))\\n    return best\\n\\n\\n@app.on_event(\\\"startup\\\")\\nasync def startup_event():\\n    await connect_swarm()\\n\\n\\n@app.get(\\\"/v1/models\\\")\\nasync def list_models():\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Список доступных моделей\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    models = [\\n        {\\n            \\\"id\\\": \\\"swarm\\\",\\n            \\\"object\\\": \\\"model\\\",\\n            \\\"created\\\": int(time.time()),\\n            \\\"owned_by\\\": \\\"swen3\\\"\\n        }\\n    ]\\n    # Добавляем отдельных воркеров\\n    for worker in AVAILABLE_WORKERS:\\n        models.append({\\n            \\\"id\\\": worker,\\n            \\\"object\\\": \\\"model\\\",\\n            \\\"created\\\": int(time.time()),\\n            \\\"owned_by\\\": \\\"swen3\\\"\\n        })\\n    \\n    return {\\n        \\\"object\\\": \\\"list\\\",\\n        \\\"data\\\": models\\n    }\\n\\n\\n@app.post(\\\"/v1/chat/completions\\\")\\nasync def chat_completions(request: ChatCompletionRequest):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Основной endpoint для чат-комплишенов\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    \\n    if not swarm_agent:\\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=503, detail=\\\"Swarm not connected\\\")\\n    \\n    question = extract_last_message(request.messages)\\n    if not question:\\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=400, detail=\\\"No user message found\\\")\\n    \\n    request_id = f\\\"chatcmpl-{uuid.uuid4().hex}\\\"\\n    created = int(time.time())\\n    \\n    # Если запрошен конкретный воркер\\n    if request.model in AVAILABLE_WORKERS:\\n        result = await ask_worker(request.model, question)\\n        \\n        if result[\\\"status\\\"] != \\\"success\\\":\\n            raise HTTPException(status_code=500, detail=result.get(\\\"error\\\", \\\"Unknown error\\\"))\\n        \\n        response = ChatCompletionResponse(\\n            id=request_id,\\n            created=created,\\n            model=request.model,\\n            choices=[\\n                ChatCompletionChoice(\\n                    index=0,\\n                    message={\\n                        \\\"role\\\": \\\"assistant\\\",\\n                        \\\"content\\\": result[\\\"answer\\\"]\\n                    },\\n                    finish_reason=\\\"stop\\\"\\n                )\\n            ],\\n            usage={\\n                \\\"prompt_tokens\\\": len(question.split()),\\n                \\\"completion_tokens\\\": len(result[\\\"answer\\\"].split()),\\n                \\\"total_tokens\\\": len(question.split()) + len(result[\\\"answer\\\"].split())\\n            }\\n        )\\n        return response\\n    \\n    # Если запрошен swarm — делаем fanout\\n    if request.model == \\\"swarm\\\":\\n        if request.stream:\\n            return StreamingResponse(\\n                stream_swarm_response(request_id, created, question),\\n                media_type=\\\"text/event-stream\\\"\\n            )\\n        else:\\n            # Non-streaming\\n            results = await fanout_to_workers(question)\\n            best = judge_best_response(results)\\n            \\n            if not best:\\n                raise HTTPException(status_code=500, detail=\\\"All workers failed\\\")\\n            \\n            response = ChatCompletionResponse(\\n                id=request_id,\\n                created=created,\\n                model=\\\"swarm\\\",\\n                choices=[\\n                    ChatCompletionChoice(\\n                        index=0,\\n                        message={\\n                            \\\"role\\\": \\\"assistant\\\",\\n                            \\\"content\\\": best[\\\"answer\\\"]\\n                        },\\n                        finish_reason=\\\"stop\\\"\\n                    )\\n                ],\\n                usage={\\n                    \\\"prompt_tokens\\\": len(question.split()),\\n                    \\\"completion_tokens\\\": len(best[\\\"answer\\\"].split()),\\n                    \\\"total_tokens\\\": len(question.split()) + len(best[\\\"answer\\\"].split())\\n                }\\n            )\\n            return response\\n    \\n    raise HTTPException(status_code=400, detail=f\\\"Unknown model: {request.model}\\\")\\n\\n\\nasync def fanout_to_workers(question: str) -> List[Dict]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Отправляет запрос всем воркерам параллельно\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    tasks = [ask_worker(worker, question) for worker in AVAILABLE_WORKERS]\\n    results = await asyncio.gather(*tasks, return_exceptions=True)\\n    \\n    processed = []\\n    for result in results:\\n        if isinstance(result, Exception):\\n            processed.append({\\n                \\\"worker\\\": \\\"unknown\\\",\\n                \\\"status\\\": \\\"error\\\",\\n                \\\"error\\\": str(result)\\n            })\\n        else:\\n            processed.append(result)\\n    \\n    return processed\\n\\n\\nasync def stream_swarm_response(request_id: str, created: int, question: str) -> AsyncGenerator[str, None]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Потоковый ответ с мышлением всех воркеров\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    \\n    # Отправляем начало\\n    yield f\\\"data: {json.dumps({'id': request_id, 'object': 'chat.completion.chunk', 'created': created, 'model': 'swarm', 'choices': [{'index': 0, 'delta': {'role': 'assistant'}, 'finish_reason': None}]})}\\\\n\\\\n\\\"\\n    \\n    # Запускаем всех воркеров\\n    tasks = {worker: asyncio.create_task(ask_worker(worker, question)) for worker in AVAILABLE_WORKERS}\\n    \\n    completed_workers = []\\n    \\n    # По мере готовности воркеров отправляем их ответы\\n    for worker in AVAILABLE_WORKERS:\\n        result = await tasks[worker]\\n        \\n        if result[\\\"status\\\"] == \\\"success\\\":\\n            # Отправляем имя воркера\\n            yield f\\\"data: {json.dumps({'id': request_id, 'object': 'chat.completion.chunk', 'created': created, 'model': 'swarm', 'choices': [{'index': 0, 'delta': {'content': f'\\\\\\\\n🤖 [{worker}]\\\\\\\\n'}, 'finish_reason': None}]})}\\\\n\\\\n\\\"\\n            \\n            # Отправляем ответ частями (для имитации потокового вывода)\\n            words = result[\\\"answer\\\"].split()\\n            chunk_size = 5\\n            for i in range(0, len(words), chunk_size):\\n                chunk = \\\" \\\".join(words[i:i+chunk_size])\\n                yield f\\\"data: {json.dumps({'id': request_id, 'object': 'chat.completion.chunk', 'created': created, 'model': 'swarm', 'choices': [{'index': 0, 'delta': {'content': chunk + ' '}, 'finish_reason': None}]})}\\\\n\\\\n\\\"\\n                await asyncio.sleep(0.05)  # Небольшая задержка для эффекта потока\\n            \\n            completed_workers.append(result)\\n        else:\\n            yield f\\\"data: {json.dumps({'id': request_id, 'object': 'chat.completion.chunk', 'created': created, 'model': 'swarm', 'choices': [{'index': 0, 'delta': {'content': f'\\\\\\\\n❌ [{worker}] failed\\\\\\\\n'}, 'finish_reason': None}]})}\\\\n\\\\n\\\"\\n    \\n    # Выбираем лучший ответ и отправляем финальный\\n    best = judge_best_response(completed_workers)\\n    if best:\\n        yield f\\\"data: {json.dumps({'id': request_id, 'object': 'chat.completion.chunk', 'created': created, 'model': 'swarm', 'choices': [{'index': 0, 'delta': {'content': f'\\\\\\\\n✅ Best: [{best[\\\\\\\"worker\\\\\\\"]}]\\\\\\\\n'}, 'finish_reason': None}]})}\\\\n\\\\n\\\"\\n    \\n    # Конец потока\\n    yield f\\\"data: {json.dumps({'id': request_id, 'object': 'chat.completion.chunk', 'created': created, 'model': 'swarm', 'choices': [{'index': 0, 'delta': {}, 'finish_reason': 'stop'}]})}\\\\n\\\\n\\\"\\n    yield \\\"data: [DONE]\\\\n\\\\n\\\"\\n\\n\\n@app.get(\\\"/health\\\")\\nasync def health_check():\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Health check endpoint\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    return {\\n        \\\"status\\\": \\\"healthy\\\",\\n        \\\"swarm_connected\\\": swarm_agent is not None,\\n        \\\"workers\\\": AVAILABLE_WORKERS\\n    }\\n\\n\\nif __name__ == \\\"__main__\\\":\\n    print(\\\"🚀 Starting SWEN v3 OpenAI-compatible API Gateway...\\\")\\n    print(f\\\"📡 Workers: {', '.join(AVAILABLE_WORKERS)}\\\")\\n    print(\\\"🔗 Endpoint: http://localhost:8080/v1/chat/completions\\\")\\n    \\n    uvicorn.run(app, host=\\\"0.0.0.0\\\", port=8080)\\n\",\"filePath\":\"/Users/alex/.local/share/swen3/openai_gateway.py\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "tool_8EBbxFimkUcHyKOp87n1KjMF", "content": "[Old tool result content cleared]"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "tool_oMksIplUtkpPhf8eBM2Gttrs", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "bash", "arguments": "{\"command\":\"cd ~/.local/share/swen3 && python3 -c \\\"import fastapi; import uvicorn; print('✅ Dependencies OK')\\\" 2>&1 || echo \\\"❌ Need to install dependencies\\\"\",\"description\":\"Check dependencies\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "tool_oMksIplUtkpPhf8eBM2Gttrs", "content": "[Old tool result content cleared]"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "tool_OGxzVIkKh5HfK6VcMhx0DEWN", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "bash", "arguments": "{\"command\":\"pip install fastapi uvicorn\",\"description\":\"Install FastAPI and uvicorn\